.TH SDL_HINT_AUDIO_ALSA_DEFAULT_DEVICE 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_AUDIO_ALSA_DEFAULT_DEVICE \- Specify the default ALSA audio device name.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_AUDIO_ALSA_DEFAULT_DEVICE \(dqSDL_AUDIO_ALSA_DEFAULT_DEVICE\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This variable is a specific audio device to open when the \(dqdefault\(dq audio device is used\[char46]
.PP
This hint will be ignored when opening the default playback device if
.BR SDL_HINT_AUDIO_ALSA_DEFAULT_PLAYBACK_DEVICE
is set, or when opening the default recording device if
.BR SDL_HINT_AUDIO_ALSA_DEFAULT_RECORDING_DEVICE
is set\[char46]
.PP
This hint should be set before an audio device is opened\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_HINT_AUDIO_ALSA_DEFAULT_PLAYBACK_DEVICE (3),
.BR SDL_HINT_AUDIO_ALSA_DEFAULT_RECORDING_DEVICE (3)
